; Logged balances, which is the only thing that gives the ledger a net-worth domain: each `balance`
; date becomes a snapshot, and every account is valued at those dates whether or not it is asserted
; here. Cards are left out for that reason — their balances come from the spending above.
;
; `pad` rather than hand-computed figures: beancount inserts whatever adjustment makes the following
; assertion true, so these numbers stay whatever the fixture says they are as the transactions above
; change. That is also the shape the app's own balance sink writes.
;
; Four dates across both years, so the year page has a series to chart and the all-time page has more
; than one year to compare.

